---
// Home: what the service is, for whom, how it differs (POSITIONING.md), and the one
// call to action. Facts come only from BRIEF.md; there is no proof yet, so the page
// explains the mechanism instead of quoting anyone.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title={SITE.name}>
  <section class="wrap hero">
    <h1>German to English technical translation for machine builders</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Operating manuals, maintenance instructions, specifications and safety notes,
      translated from German into English by a mechanical engineer, in your own
      terminology, at a fixed price agreed before work starts.
    </p>
    <p class="cta">
      <a class="button" href="/contact">Ask for a fixed price</a>
      <a href="/services">See what is translated and how</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Who this is for</h2>
    <p>
      You write or manage technical documentation at a small or mid-size machine
      builder in Germany. Your machines sell abroad, and every one of them needs an
      English manual. Fernwood Technical Translation does one thing: technical
      translation for machine builders, from German into English.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What you might use today</h2>
      <ul class="cards">
        <li>
          <h3>Machine translation</h3>
          <p>Fast, but one of your own engineers then reviews every page and corrects the technical terms.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>A large agency</h3>
          <p>Many translators across many subjects. The person on your next manual may not be the one on your last.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>A generalist freelancer</h3>
          <p>Translates many kinds of text. Machine documentation is one subject among several.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>What is different here</h2>
    <ul class="cards">
      <li>
        <h3>An engineer who translates</h3>
        <p>Jo Fernwood trained as a mechanical engineer, so the translation starts from how the machine works.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Only machine documentation</h3>
        <p>Operating manuals, maintenance instructions, specifications and safety notes. No other kind of text.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Your terminology, kept</h3>
        <p>You send a terminology list, or Jo builds one with you on the first job. It is used on every later job.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>A fixed price first</h3>
        <p>The work is priced per word. You agree one fixed price before any work starts.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What that gives you</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Fewer review rounds for your own engineers, because the translator already understands the machine.</li>
        <li>The same English word for the same part, in every manual you publish.</li>
        <li>A known translation cost before the job begins.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="cta">
        <a class="button" href="/contact">Ask for a fixed price</a>
        <a href="/about">About Jo Fernwood</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
